Crates kept here with a change of Swarm's, each with its own licences.

i-slint-backend-android-activity: Slint 1.18.1's Android backend, its
licences in LICENSES/, with two changes in java/SlintAndroidJavaHelper.java:
- a keyboard's connection replaced (a field's type changed, as the
  passphrase's eye does) ends any batch of edits it had begun, so what's
  typed still reaches the window afterwards;
- in a password field, what the keyboard is still composing is given to
  the window as typed, not as a preedit, so a keyboard that composes even
  in password fields doesn't leave the last word out of the passphrase.
Test for both: tools/test-android-input.sh, on a phone over adb.

i-slint-core: Slint 1.18.1's core, its licences in LICENSES/, with one
change in items/text.rs (StyledTextItem::input_event): a press, a move or
a release that isn't on a link, or isn't the left button's, is passed on
to what's beneath. A chat line with web addresses lays its links over the
same text plain (desktop/ui/parts.slint, Links), which can then still be
dragged over to select it, long-pressed on the phone to copy it, and
right-clicked for its menu.
Tests: desktop's a_chat_line_with_a_link_dragged_over_is_copied and
on_the_phone_a_link_opens_and_its_line_still_copies.

quinn-proto: quinn-proto 0.11.19, its licences in LICENSE-APACHE and
LICENSE-MIT, with one setting added, TransportConfig::max_probe_interval
(src/config/transport.rs, used in src/connection/mod.rs's
pto_time_and_space): the longest an established connection waits between
probes while what it's sent goes unanswered, however long the round trip's
been reckoned (never under the quickest seen). Without it QUIC doubles
the wait after each probe, so a link gone for a few seconds (a Wi-Fi roam)
and back would go unprobed for seconds more. Swarm sets it in
core/src/transport.rs. Capped, the wait is counted from the last probe
timeout as well as from the last ack-eliciting packet
(Connection::last_pto), so probes never pile up while the socket can't
take them.
Tests: core/tests/calls.rs,
a_call_goes_on_at_its_rate_after_the_link_drops_for_a_moment, and
src/tests/mod.rs,
capped_probe_interval_does_not_pile_up_probes_while_nothing_can_be_sent
(quinn-proto's own tests run from a copy with an empty [workspace] table
added to its Cargo.toml).

Moving any of them to a newer version: fetch the new release's source
(`cargo download`, or the .crate from crates.io, unpacked), make a diff
of the change here against the release it was made on (the old .crate
unpacked beside it: `diff -ru old vendor/<crate>`, leaving out .cargo-ok,
.cargo_vcs_info.json and Cargo.toml.orig), apply that diff to the new
source, put it in place of vendor/<crate>, bump the version named above
and in the workspace's Cargo.lock (`cargo update -p <crate>`), and run
the change's tests. Slint's backend and core move with the slint version
desktop/ and android/ use; check first whether the new release has the
change already, and if so drop the patch and its [patch.crates-io] line.
